## Steps — send mode

1. Build today's plan from {% if use_kb %}the `kb next` tasks{% else %}`state.md` WIP items{% endif %} + the user's input; estimate
   each (~6 focused h/day budget). Thin evidence → "low confidence".
2. Show the draft plan + the remaining items; loop swaps until an explicit go.
3. Build the Teams message (HTML, **always English**) — same format as the
   tracked variant, one `<li>` per planned item with estimate, no links.
4. Check `mcp__claude_ai_Microsoft_365__get_me` matches the identity {{ identity }}'s
   "Teams account must be"; on a mismatch or an auth error the Microsoft 365
   connector needs reconnecting in claude.ai under Customize → Connectors —
   stop and tell the user
   (`teams-message` skill, Send step 1). Send via
   `mcp__claude_ai_Microsoft_365__teams_send_chat_message` to the identity
   {{ identity }}'s status chatId, `bodyType: "html"`. Report the message id.

## Write rules

- Teams: **always English**; exactly one message per explicit go, to the
  identity {{ identity }}'s chat only; shaping and sending per the `teams-message` skill.
  (`rebalance` mode is N/A without a ticket tracker.)
{% endif %}
